t\" class=\"block\">\n  \n    \n      <div class=\"block-content\">\n      <article data-history-node-id=\"32\" class=\"contextual-region node node-type-page node-view-mode-full\">\n  <header class=\"node-header\">\n    \n        <div data-contextual-id=\"node:node=32:changed=1769163082&amp;langcode=en\" data-contextual-token=\"umDMVG4n6u8yImD2fmzflMKZbzfkIhRmFFIKqTxFGbg\" data-drupal-ajax-container=\"\"></div>\n      </header>\n  <div class=\"node-content\">\n    <div class=\"field field-name-body field-type-text-with-summary field-label-hidden\">\n            <div class=\"field field-name-body field-type-text-with-summary field-label-hidden field-item\"><p>This activity aims to migrate labs that use proprietary software (e.g. OrCAD, PSpice) to eSim. eSim is free/libre and open source and offers the same capabilities for circuit design, simulation, analysis, and PCB design as any other proprietary EDA tool. Hence educational institutions can save a huge amount of money that they may spend on procuring licenses.</p><p>We invite students and faculty from all Engineering Colleges to come forward and take part in this activity. The Lab Migration team helps in the following ways:</p><ul><li>Provide suggestions on the different ways eSim can be implemented in the laboratory.</li><li>Coordinate the migration of the lab to a FLOSS-only laboratory.</li><li>Provide solutions to the lab\'s problem statements.</li><li>Conduct eSim workshops free of cost.</li></ul></div>\n      </div>\n  </div>\n</article>\n\n    </div><!--/block-content -->\n  </div><!--/block -->\n\n  </div>\n\n              </main>\n              <div id=\"sidebar-left\" class=\"sidebar\">\n  <aside class=\"sidebar-left\" role=\"complementary\">\n      <div class=\"block-region region-sidebar-left\">\n    <drupal-render-placeholder callback=\"Drupal\\block\\BlockViewBuilder::lazyBuilder\" arguments=\"0=nava_labmigrationproject&amp;1=full&amp;2\" token=\"8U6H2gzmJ0lslIoxuuwq2Lrhvu7cEaAE8TlN6R9sptY\"></drupal-