('page',	0,	18,	25,	'en',	0,	'<p>&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Please address your queries/suggestions to:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<br>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.che.iitb.ac.in/online/node/52\" target=\"_blank\"&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prof. Kannan M. Moudgalya&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt; of Chemical Engineering,&lt;/p&gt;<br>&lt;p&gt;Indian Institute of Technology Bombay, Powai,&lt;/p&gt;<br>&lt;p&gt;Mumbai - 400076&lt;/p&gt;<br>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;img src=\"https://www.clker.com/cliparts/0/f/c/2/1195445181899094722molumen_phone_icon.svg.med.png\" alt=\"\" /&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;strong&gt;022-2576- 4133 &lt;/strong&gt;[10.00 AM - 6.00 PM]&lt;/p&gt;<br>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;For queries mail us at :&lt;/strong&gt; contact-r(at)fossee(dot)in&lt;/p&gt;<br>&lt;p&gt;For more details please visit &lt;a href=\"https://fossee.in\"&gt;fossee.in&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<br>&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;</p>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	18,	26,	'en',	0,	'<p class=\"rtejustify\"><u>Please address your queries/suggestions to:</u></p><p class=\"rtejustify\"><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://www.che.iitb.ac.in/online/node/52\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><u>Prof. Kannan M. Moudgalya</u></strong></a> of Chemical Engineering,</p><p class=\"rtejustify\">Indian Institute of Technology Bombay, Powai,</p><p class=\"rtejustify\">Mumbai - 400076</p><p class=\"rtejustify\">&nbsp;<img style=\"border-width:0;\" src=\"https://www.clker.com/cliparts/0/f/c/2/1195445181899094722molumen_phone_icon.svg.med.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> &nbsp;<strong>022-2576- 4133 </strong>[10.00 AM - 6.00 PM]</p><p class=\"rtejustify\"><strong>For queries mail us at :</strong> contact-r(at)fossee(dot)in</p><p class=\"rtejustify\">For more details please visit <a href=\"https://fossee.in\">fossee.in</a></p><p class=\"rtejustify\">&nbsp;</p>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	18,	27,	'en',	0,	'<p class=\"rtejustify\"><u>Please address your queries/suggestions to:</u></p><p class=\"rtejustify\"><a class=\"ext\" href=\"https://www.che.iitb.ac.in/online/node/52\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><u>Prof. Kannan M. Moudgalya</u></strong></a> of Chemical Engineering,</p><p class=\"rtejustify\">Indian Institute of Technology Bombay, Powai,</p><p class=\"rtejustify\">Mumbai - 400076</p><p class=\"rtejustify\">&nbsp;<img style=\"border-width:0;\" src=\"https://www.clker.com/cliparts/0/f/c/2/1195445181899094722molumen_phone_icon.svg.med.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> &nbsp;<strong>022-2576- 4133 </strong>[10.00 AM - 6.00 PM]</p><p class=\"rtejustify\"><strong>For queries mail us at :</strong> contact-r(at)fossee(dot)in</p><p class=\"rtejustify\">For more details please visit <a href=\"https://fossee.in\">fossee.in</a></p><p class=\"rtejustify\">&nbsp;</p>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	20,	29,	'en',	0,	'<p>FreeCAD</p><p>Versatile 3D modeler</p>',	'',	'basic_html'),
('page',	0,	21,	30,	'en',	0,	'<p>FreeCAD</p><p>Versatile 3D modeler</p>',	'',	'basic_html'),
('page',	0,	23,	32,	'en',	0,	'<p><strong>The Spoken Tutorial project is about teaching and learning a particular FLOSS (Free/Libre and Open Source Software) like Linux, Scilab, LaTeX, PHP &amp; MySQL, Java, C/C++, LibreOffice etc. via an easy video tool - Spoken Tutorial. A Spoken Tutorial is a screencast with running commentary, a recording of computer session created for self learning. Each Spoken Tutorial typically runs for a duration of approximately ten minutes. Using these Spoken Tutorials, one can conduct SELF (Spoken Tutorial based Education and Learning through Free FLOSS study) workshops.</strong></p><p><strong>The Spoken Tutorial project was established under the National Mission on Education through Information and Communication Technology, launched by MHRD, Govt of India.</strong></p><p>Click here https://spoken-tutorial.org/tutorial-search/?search_foss=FreeCAD&amp;search_language=English to access all the FreeCAD Spoken Tutorials</p><p><br><br>&nbsp;</p>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	24,	33,	'en',	0,	'<p><strong>The Spoken Tutorial project is about teaching and learning a particular FLOSS (Free/Libre and Open Source Software) like Linux, Scilab, LaTeX, PHP &amp; MySQL, Java, C/C++, LibreOffice etc. via an easy video tool - Spoken Tutorial. A Spoken Tutorial is a screencast with running commentary, a recording of computer session created for self learning. Each Spoken Tutorial typically runs for a duration of approximately ten minutes. Using these Spoken Tutorials, one can conduct SELF (Spoken Tutorial based Education and Learning through Free FLOSS study) workshops.</strong></p><p><strong>The Spoken Tutorial project was established under the National Mission on Education through Information and Communication Technology, launched by MHRD, Govt of India.</strong></p><p>Click here https://spoken-tutorial.org/tutorial-search/?search_foss=FreeCAD&amp;search_language=English to access all the FreeCAD Spoken Tutorials</p><p><br><br>&nbsp;</p>',	'',	'basic_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	36,	'en',	0,	'<p class=\"text-align-justify\">FreeCAD is an open-source parametric 3D CAD (Computer-Aided Design) modeller primarily aimed at mechanical engineering and product design. It allows users to create and design models of any size, making it perfect for detailed mechanical parts and optimizing designs for 3D printing. Backed by a vibrant community, FreeCAD continues to evolve, offering a robust platform for 3D design and engineering projects.</p>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	37,	'en',	0,	'<h3 class=\"text-align-justify\">Introduction:</h3><p class=\"text-align-justify\">FreeCAD is an open-source parametric 3D CAD (Computer-Aided Design) modeller primarily aimed at mechanical engineering and product design. It allows users to create and design models of any size, making it perfect for detailed mechanical parts and optimizing designs for 3D printing. Backed by a vibrant community, FreeCAD continues to evolve, offering a robust platform for 3D design and engineering projects.</p>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	49,	'en',	0,	'<h3 class=\"text-align-justify\">Introduction:</h3><p class=\"text-align-justify\">FreeCAD is an open-source parametric 3D CAD (Computer-Aided Design) modeller primarily aimed at mechanical engineering and product design. It allows users to create and design models of any size, making it perfect for detailed mechanical parts and optimizing designs for 3D printing. Backed by a vibrant community, FreeCAD continues to evolve, offering a robust platform for 3D design and engineering projects.</p>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	50,	'en',	0,	'<h3 class=\"text-align-justify\">Introduction:</h3><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">FreeCAD is a powerful, open-source 3D modeling tool designed for everyone from hobbyists to professional engineers and architects. It allows users to create real-life objects with various tools and features, including 3D modelling, drafting, simulation, and rendering capabilities.</p>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	51,	'en',	0,	'<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>FreeCAD</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Versatile 3D modeler</strong></p><p style=\"font-weight:normal;line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:14pt;\" size=\"4\" color=\"#000000\"><strong>Introduction:</strong></font></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font color=\"#000000\">FreeCAD is an open-source parametric 3D CAD (Computer-Aided Design) modeller primarily aimed at mechanical engineering and product design. It allows users to create and design models of any size, making it perfect for detailed mechanical parts and optimizing designs for 3D printing. Backed by a vibrant community, FreeCAD continues to evolve, offering a robust platform for 3D design and engineering projects.</font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:14pt;\" color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Parametric Modeling</strong>: Easily modify your design by going back into your model history and changing its parameters.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Modular Architecture</strong>: Customize FreeCAD by adding or removing plugins to fit your specific needs.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Sketcher Workbench</strong>: Create precise 2D sketches using constraints and use them as a base for building 3D models.</font></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Part and Assembly Design</strong>: Design and assemble complex parts and assemblies.</font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Path Workbench (CAM):</strong> Generate G-code for CNC machines directly from your models.</font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Robot Simulation: </strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\">Simulate robot movements in a 3D environment to plan and verify robotic operations.</span></font></p><p style=\"font-weight:normal;line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Rendering :</strong> Export models to rendering software like Blender for high-quality visualizations.</font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Multi-Platform</strong>: Runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux, providing a consistent experience across different operating systems.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Open Source</strong>: Completely free to use and modify, with a large, active community contributing to its development.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Supports Various File Formats</strong>: Import and export a wide range of formats including STEP, IGES, STL, SVG, DXF, OBJ, IFC, and more.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Built-In Python Interpreter</strong>: Automate tasks and extend functionality through scripting.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Customizable Interface</strong>: Adapt the user interface to suit your workflow with customizable toolbars and workspaces.</font></li></ul><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>\"In the realm of open-source CAD solutions, FreeCAD stands out for its versatility and robust design capabilities. It’s a fantastic resource for engineers and designers across India.\"</strong> – <strong>Dr. Anil Kumar</strong>, Director of Engineering, TCS</font></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>click here to download </strong></font><a href=\"https://www.freecad.org/\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>https://www.freecad.org/</strong></font></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	52,	'en',	0,	'<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>FreeCAD &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Versatile 3D modeler</strong></p><p style=\"font-weight:normal;line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><strong>Introduction:</strong></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font color=\"#000000\">FreeCAD is an open-source parametric 3D CAD (Computer-Aided Design) modeller primarily aimed at mechanical engineering and product design. It allows users to create and design models of any size, making it perfect for detailed mechanical parts and optimizing designs for 3D printing. Backed by a vibrant community, FreeCAD continues to evolve, offering a robust platform for 3D design and engineering projects.</font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:14pt;\" color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Parametric Modeling</strong>: Easily modify your design by going back into your model history and changing its parameters.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Modular Architecture</strong>: Customize FreeCAD by adding or removing plugins to fit your specific needs.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Sketcher Workbench</strong>: Create precise 2D sketches using constraints and use them as a base for building 3D models.</font></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Part and Assembly Design</strong>: Design and assemble complex parts and assemblies.</font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Path Workbench (CAM):</strong> Generate G-code for CNC machines directly from your models.</font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Robot Simulation: </strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\">Simulate robot movements in a 3D environment to plan and verify robotic operations.</span></font></p><p style=\"font-weight:normal;line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Rendering :</strong> Export models to rendering software like Blender for high-quality visualizations.</font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Multi-Platform</strong>: Runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux, providing a consistent experience across different operating systems.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Open Source</strong>: Completely free to use and modify, with a large, active community contributing to its development.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Supports Various File Formats</strong>: Import and export a wide range of formats including STEP, IGES, STL, SVG, DXF, OBJ, IFC, and more.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Built-In Python Interpreter</strong>: Automate tasks and extend functionality through scripting.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Customizable Interface</strong>: Adapt the user interface to suit your workflow with customizable toolbars and workspaces.</font></li></ul><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>\"In the realm of open-source CAD solutions, FreeCAD stands out for its versatility and robust design capabilities. It’s a fantastic resource for engineers and designers across India.\"</strong> – <strong>Dr. Anil Kumar</strong>, Director of Engineering, TCS</font></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>click here to download </strong></font><a href=\"https://www.freecad.org/\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>https://www.freecad.org/</strong></font></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	53,	'en',	0,	'<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>FreeCAD &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<strong> Versatile 3D modeler</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p style=\"font-weight:normal;line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font color=\"#000000\">FreeCAD is an open-source parametric 3D CAD (Computer-Aided Design) modeller primarily aimed at mechanical engineering and product design. It allows users to create and design models of any size, making it perfect for detailed mechanical parts and optimizing designs for 3D printing. Backed by a vibrant community, FreeCAD continues to evolve, offering a robust platform for 3D design and engineering projects.</font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:14pt;\" color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Parametric Modeling</strong>: Easily modify your design by going back into your model history and changing its parameters.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Modular Architecture</strong>: Customize FreeCAD by adding or removing plugins to fit your specific needs.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Sketcher Workbench</strong>: Create precise 2D sketches using constraints and use them as a base for building 3D models.</font></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Part and Assembly Design</strong>: Design and assemble complex parts and assemblies.</font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Path Workbench (CAM):</strong> Generate G-code for CNC machines directly from your models.</font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Robot Simulation: </strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\">Simulate robot movements in a 3D environment to plan and verify robotic operations.</span></font></p><p style=\"font-weight:normal;line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Rendering :</strong> Export models to rendering software like Blender for high-quality visualizations.</font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Multi-Platform</strong>: Runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux, providing a consistent experience across different operating systems.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Open Source</strong>: Completely free to use and modify, with a large, active community contributing to its development.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Supports Various File Formats</strong>: Import and export a wide range of formats including STEP, IGES, STL, SVG, DXF, OBJ, IFC, and more.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Built-In Python Interpreter</strong>: Automate tasks and extend functionality through scripting.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Customizable Interface</strong>: Adapt the user interface to suit your workflow with customizable toolbars and workspaces.</font></li></ul><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>\"In the realm of open-source CAD solutions, FreeCAD stands out for its versatility and robust design capabilities. It’s a fantastic resource for engineers and designers across India.\"</strong> – <strong>Dr. Anil Kumar</strong>, Director of Engineering, TCS</font></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>click here to download </strong></font><a href=\"https://www.freecad.org/\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>https://www.freecad.org/</strong></font></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	57,	'en',	0,	'<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<strong>FreeCAD &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<strong> Versatile 3D modeler</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p style=\"font-weight:normal;line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font color=\"#000000\">FreeCAD is an open-source parametric 3D CAD (Computer-Aided Design) modeller primarily aimed at mechanical engineering and product design. It allows users to create and design models of any size, making it perfect for detailed mechanical parts and optimizing designs for 3D printing. Backed by a vibrant community, FreeCAD continues to evolve, offering a robust platform for 3D design and engineering projects.</font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:14pt;\" color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></font></p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Parametric Modeling</strong>: Easily modify your design by going back into your model history and changing its parameters.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Modular Architecture</strong>: Customize FreeCAD by adding or removing plugins to fit your specific needs.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Sketcher Workbench</strong>: Create precise 2D sketches using constraints and use them as a base for building 3D models.</font></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Part and Assembly Design</strong>: Design and assemble complex parts and assemblies.</font></p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Path Workbench (CAM):</strong> Generate G-code for CNC machines directly from your models.</font></p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Robot Simulation: </strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\">Simulate robot movements in a 3D environment to plan and verify robotic operations.</span></font></p><p style=\"font-weight:normal;line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Rendering :</strong> Export models to rendering software like Blender for high-quality visualizations.</font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Multi-Platform</strong>: Runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux, providing a consistent experience across different operating systems.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Open Source</strong>: Completely free to use and modify, with a large, active community contributing to its development.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Supports Various File Formats</strong>: Import and export a wide range of formats including STEP, IGES, STL, SVG, DXF, OBJ, IFC, and more.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Built-In Python Interpreter</strong>: Automate tasks and extend functionality through scripting.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Customizable Interface</strong>: Adapt the user interface to suit your workflow with customizable toolbars and workspaces.</font></li></ul><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>\"In the realm of open-source CAD solutions, FreeCAD stands out for its versatility and robust design capabilities. It’s a fantastic resource for engineers and designers across India.\"</strong> – <strong>Dr. Anil Kumar</strong>, Director of Engineering, TCS</font></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>click here to download </strong></font><a href=\"https://www.freecad.org/\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>https://www.freecad.org/</strong></font></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	58,	'en',	0,	'<p class=\"text-align-center\"><strong>FreeCAD &nbsp;Versatile 3D modeler &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>&nbsp;</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p class=\"text-align-justify\"><font color=\"#000000\">FreeCAD is an open-source parametric 3D CAD (Computer-Aided Design) modeller primarily aimed at mechanical engineering and product design. It allows users to create and design models of any size, making it perfect for detailed mechanical parts and optimizing designs for 3D printing. Backed by a vibrant community, FreeCAD continues to evolve, offering a robust platform for 3D design and engineering projects.</font></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:14pt;\" color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></font></p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Parametric Modeling</strong>: Easily modify your design by going back into your model history and changing its parameters.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Modular Architecture</strong>: Customize FreeCAD by adding or removing plugins to fit your specific needs.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Sketcher Workbench</strong>: Create precise 2D sketches using constraints and use them as a base for building 3D models.</font></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Part and Assembly Design</strong>: Design and assemble complex parts and assemblies.</font></p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Path Workbench (CAM):</strong> Generate G-code for CNC machines directly from your models.</font></p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Robot Simulation: </strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\">Simulate robot movements in a 3D environment to plan and verify robotic operations.</span></font></p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Rendering :</strong> Export models to rendering software like Blender for high-quality visualizations.</font></p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Multi-Platform</strong>: Runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux, providing a consistent experience across different operating systems.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Open Source</strong>: Completely free to use and modify, with a large, active community contributing to its development.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Supports Various File Formats</strong>: Import and export a wide range of formats including STEP, IGES, STL, SVG, DXF, OBJ, IFC, and more.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Built-In Python Interpreter</strong>: Automate tasks and extend functionality through scripting.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Customizable Interface</strong>: Adapt the user interface to suit your workflow with customizable toolbars and workspaces.</font></li></ul><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>\"In the realm of open-source CAD solutions, FreeCAD stands out for its versatility and robust design capabilities. It’s a fantastic resource for engineers and designers across India.\"</strong> – <strong>Dr. Anil Kumar</strong>, Director of Engineering, TCS</font></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>click here to download </strong></font><a href=\"https://www.freecad.org/\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>https://www.freecad.org/</strong></font></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	26,	65,	'en',	0,	'<p class=\"text-align-center\"><strong>FreeCAD &nbsp;Versatile 3D modeler &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>&nbsp;</strong> &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p class=\"text-align-justify\"><font color=\"#000000\">FreeCAD is an open-source parametric 3D CAD (Computer-Aided Design) modeller primarily aimed at mechanical engineering and product design. It allows users to create and design models of any size, making it perfect for detailed mechanical parts and optimizing designs for 3D printing. Backed by a vibrant community, FreeCAD continues to evolve, offering a robust platform for 3D design and engineering projects.</font></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:14pt;\" color=\"#000000\" size=\"4\"><strong>Key Features:</strong></font></p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Parametric Modeling</strong>: Easily modify your design by going back into your model history and changing its parameters.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Modular Architecture</strong>: Customize FreeCAD by adding or removing plugins to fit your specific needs.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Sketcher Workbench</strong>: Create precise 2D sketches using constraints and use them as a base for building 3D models.</font></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Part and Assembly Design</strong>: Design and assemble complex parts and assemblies.</font></p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Path Workbench (CAM):</strong> Generate G-code for CNC machines directly from your models.</font></p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Robot Simulation: </strong><span style=\"font-weight:normal;\">Simulate robot movements in a 3D environment to plan and verify robotic operations.</span></font></p></li><li><p style=\"line-height:100%;margin-bottom:0in;\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Rendering :</strong> Export models to rendering software like Blender for high-quality visualizations.</font></p></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Multi-Platform</strong>: Runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux, providing a consistent experience across different operating systems.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Open Source</strong>: Completely free to use and modify, with a large, active community contributing to its development.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Supports Various File Formats</strong>: Import and export a wide range of formats including STEP, IGES, STL, SVG, DXF, OBJ, IFC, and more.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Built-In Python Interpreter</strong>: Automate tasks and extend functionality through scripting.</font></li><li><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>Customizable Interface</strong>: Adapt the user interface to suit your workflow with customizable toolbars and workspaces.</font></li></ul><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>\"In the realm of open-source CAD solutions, FreeCAD stands out for its versatility and robust design capabilities. It’s a fantastic resource for engineers and designers across India.\"</strong> – <strong>Dr. Anil Kumar</strong>, Director of Engineering, TCS</font></p><ul><li style=\"display:block;\"><p><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>click here to download </strong></font><a href=\"https://www.freecad.org/\"><font style=\"font-size:12pt;\" face=\"Liberation Sans, sans-serif\" size=\"3\"><strong>https://www.freecad.org/</strong></font></a></p><p>&nbsp;</p></li></ul>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	32,	62,	'en',	0,	'<h6>This activity aims to migrate labs that use proprietary software (e.g. OrCAD, PSpice) to eSim. eSim is free/libre and open source and offers the same capabilities for circuit design, simulation, analysis, and PCB design as any other proprietary EDA tool. Hence educational institutions can save a huge amount of money that they may spend on procuring licenses.</h6><h6>We invite students and faculty from all Engineering Colleges to come forward and take part in this activity. The Lab Migration team helps in the following ways:</h6><ul><li><h6>Provide suggestions on the different ways eSim can be implemented in the laboratory.</h6></li><li><h6>Coordinate the migration of the lab to a <strong>FLOSS-only</strong> laboratory.</h6></li><li><h6>Provide solutions to the lab\'s problem statements.</h6></li><li><h6>Conduct eSim workshops free of cost.</h6></li></ul>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	32,	63,	'en',	0,	'<h6>This activity aims to migrate labs that use proprietary software (e.g. OrCAD, PSpice) to eSim. eSim is free/libre and open source and offers the same capabilities for circuit design, simulation, analysis, and PCB design as any other proprietary EDA tool. Hence educational institutions can save a huge amount of money that they may spend on procuring licenses.</h6><h6>We invite students and faculty from all Engineering Colleges to come forward and take part in this activity. The Lab Migration team helps in the following ways:</h6><ul><li><h6>Provide suggestions on the different ways eSim can be implemented in the laboratory.</h6></li><li><h6>Coordinate the migration of the lab to a <strong>FLOSS-only</strong> laboratory.</h6></li><li><h6>Provide solutions to the lab\'s problem statements.</h6></li><li><h6>Conduct eSim workshops free of cost.</h6></li></ul>',	'',	'full_html'),
('page',	0,	32,	64,	'en',	0,	'<p>This activity aims to migrate labs that use proprietary software (e.g. OrCAD, PSpice) to eSim. eSim is free/libre and open source and offers the same capabilities for circuit design, simulation, analysis, and PCB design as any other proprietary EDA tool. Hence educational institutions can save a huge amount of money that they may spend on procuring licenses.</p><p>We invite students and faculty from all Engineering Colleges to come forward and take part in this activity. The Lab Migration team helps in the following ways:</p><ul><li>Provide suggestions on the different ways eSim can be implemented in the laboratory.</li><li>Coordinate the migration of the lab to a FLOSS-only laboratory.</li><li>Provide solutions to the lab\'s problem statements.</li><li>Conduct eSim workshops free of cost.</li></ul>',	'',	'full_html');
